From: Claude <ID+AndrewVSutherland2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 21:56:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] README: typo and hygiene fixes in the definition

- 'thie' -> 'this'; $m_ip_{i+i}$ -> $m_ip_{i+1}$; lowercase $a_i$ -> $A_i$.
- n is defined once, from p_0 (the first bullet said p_i, the third p_0).
- $A_i\ne\pm2$ and $B_i$ arbitrary -> gcd(A_i^2-4, p_i) = gcd(B_i, p_i) = 1, so
  that the reduction really is an elliptic curve modulo every prime divisor of
  p_i, which is where the order condition and the Hasse bound are applied.
  Both are single gcds for a verifier (voneshot.py checks the same for A).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
